Diana,

We completed the field STC testing on the mock-up unit walls last week. Results are below:

Test Location 1 (Unit 4A/4B demising wall): STC 47
Test Location 2 (Unit 4B/4C demising wall): STC 48
Test Location 3 (Unit 4A/corridor wall): STC 52

As noted in RFI-017, the code requires STC 50 between residential units. We're falling short at both unit-to-unit test locations.

The acoustical consultant recommends the following modifications:
1. Add resilient channel to one side of the demising wall (+3 STC points)
2. Increase batt insulation from 3.5" to 6" (+1-2 STC points)
3. Add a layer of 5/8" Type X gypsum to one side (+2 STC points)

Option 1 alone should get us to STC 50-51, which meets code. Cost impact is approximately $85 per linear foot of demising wall, or roughly $340,000 for all 200 units.

Options 2+3 combined would achieve STC 52-53 but at $520,000.

We need a decision by April 26th to maintain the drywall schedule on floors 3-5. Can you discuss with the owner and get back to us?

